Metadata: {"id": "Y53", "fqn": "GourResource.gsl_y53", "source": {"gour": {"ref": "Thm 11.4", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.05474v2#nameddest=theorem.11.4", "page": 504}, "hy": [{"ref": "Thm 1", "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2408.02722v3#Thmtheorem1"}, {"ref": "Thm 4", "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2408.02722v3#Thmtheorem4"}]}, "statement": "If the family of free-state sets satisfies the three conditions (closedness and convexity, closedness under tensor products, and existence of a positive definite free state), then for every fixed $\\epsilon\\in(0,1)$ the composite testing rate $b_n^\\epsilon$ converges to $D^{\\mathrm{reg}}(\\rho\\Vert F)$. Permutation invariance and closedness under partial traces are not assumed.", "book": "Convergence of the composite testing rate [corresponds to H–Y Theorem 1; used in this formalization in the proof of the declaration corresponding to Gour Theorem 11.4]", "original": {"gour": "\\begin{myt}{\\color{yellow} The Generalized Quantum Stein's Lemma}\n\\begin{theorem}\\label{gsl}\nLet $\\mf$ be a QRT whose sets of free states satisfy the properties above.\nThen, for all $\\eps\\in(0,1)$ and all $\\rho\\in\\md(A)$\n\\be\\label{1158}\n\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{1}{n}D_{\\min}^{\\eps}\\left(\\rho^{\\otimes n}\\big\\|\\mf\\right)=D^{\\reg}(\\rho\\|\\mf)\\;.\n\\ee\n\\end{theorem}", "hy": "\\begin{theorem}[\\label{thm:main_generalized_steins_lemma}Generalized quantum Stein's lemma]\nGiven any family $\\mathcal{F}$ of sets of states satisfying Properties~\\ref{p1:main}--\\ref{p2:main}, any state $\\rho$ of $\\mathcal{H}$, and any target type I error $\\epsilon\\in(0,1)$,\nthe optimal exponent of type II error is\n\\begin{align}\n\\label{eq:stein_main}\n    \\lim_{n\\to\\infty}-\\frac{\\log\\qty(\\min_{T_n}\\max_{\\sigma\\in\\mathcal{F}\\qty(\\mathcal{H}^{\\otimes n})}\\Tr\\qty[T_n\\sigma])}{n}= R_\\mathrm{R}^\\infty(\\rho),\n\\end{align}\nwhere the minimum is taken over all POVMs $\\qty{T_n,\\mathds{1}-T_n}$ suppressing the type I error below $\\epsilon$, i.e., $\\Tr[\\qty(\\mathds{1}-T_n)\\rho^{\\otimes n}]\\leq\\epsilon$, and $R_\\mathrm{R}^\\infty$ is the regularized relative entropy of resource.\n\\end{theorem}"}, "signature_sha256": "70358188dc55d5b530192caa489847e6360ac2c578c37becb55ebfd083c7a1c8", "display": {"section": "hy", "statement": "Under the three conditions (closedness and convexity, closedness under tensor products, and existence of a positive definite free state), $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}b_n^\\epsilon=D^{\\mathrm{reg}}(\\rho\\Vert F)$ for every fixed $\\epsilon\\in(0,1)$, where $b_n^\\epsilon$ is the composite testing rate. Permutation invariance and closedness under partial traces are not assumed."}, "numbered_source": true}
