bel{eq:stein_main}\n    \\lim_{n\\to\\infty}-\\frac{\\log\\qty(\\min_{T_n}\\max_{\\sigma\\in\\mathcal{F}\\qty(\\mathcal{H}^{\\otimes n})}\\Tr\\qty[T_n\\sigma])}{n}= R_\\mathrm{R}^\\infty(\\rho),\n\\end{align}\nwhere the minimum is taken over all POVMs $\\qty{T_n,\\mathds{1}-T_n}$ suppressing the type I error below $\\epsilon$, i.e., $\\Tr[\\qty(\\mathds{1}-T_n)\\rho^{\\otimes n}]\\leq\\epsilon$, and $R_\\mathrm{R}^\\infty$ is the regularized relative entropy of resource."}, "signature_sha256": "bd6806fcae8296988256e4e2bff631b4ce2fffcae1367892d6225f1cc574be59", "display": {"section": "foundation", "statement": "The rate that is $h_n^\\epsilon=\\frac{1}{n}\\inf_{\\sigma\\in F_n}D_{\\min}^{\\epsilon}(\\rho^{\\otimes n}\\Vert\\sigma)$ for $n\\geq1$ and 0 for $n=0$. The optimal type-II error $\\beta$ is defined as a real infimum, and with the negative logarithm of $\\beta\\leq0$ and the infimum over an empty free-state set taken to be $+\\infty$, the value is defined for every real $\\epsilon$."}, "numbered_source": false}
