Metadata: {"id": "B04", "fqn": "GourResource.gsl_b04", "source": {"gour": {"ref": "Thm 11.4 (where it is used; the bridge has no counterpart in the source (foundation))", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.05474v2#nameddest=theorem.11.4", "page": 504}, "hy": []}, "statement": "For pairs of density operators of the standard model, gives the correspondence and isometric transport of the trace distance and the square-root fidelity. It gives contraction under quantum channels, the bound of the trace distance by the square root of 1 minus the square of the square-root fidelity, and the distance formula for pure states given by pairs of unit vectors.", "book": "Correspondence with finite-dimensional models: trace distance, root fidelity and a Fuchs–van de Graaf type upper bound [foundation; no separate theorem number]", "original": {"gour": "\\begin{myt}{\\color{yellow} The Generalized Quantum Stein's Lemma}\n\\begin{theorem}\\label{gsl}\nLet $\\mf$ be a QRT whose sets of free states satisfy the properties above.\nThen, for all $\\eps\\in(0,1)$ and all $\\rho\\in\\md(A)$\n\\be\\label{1158}\n\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{1}{n}D_{\\min}^{\\eps}\\left(\\rho^{\\otimes n}\\big\\|\\mf\\right)=D^{\\reg}(\\rho\\|\\mf)\\;.\n\\ee\n\\end{theorem}", "hy": ""}, "signature_sha256": "ad889f9b442cd34c42c18128a8211eab70e720dd0c6cd229b909851558f0d0e4", "display": {"section": "foundation", "statement": "For pairs of density operators of the standard model, gives the correspondence and isometric transport of the trace distance and the square-root fidelity. It gives contraction under quantum channels, the bound of the trace distance by the square root of 1 minus the square of the square-root fidelity, and the distance formula for pure states given by pairs of unit vectors."}, "numbered_source": false}
