Metadata: {"id": "B05", "fqn": "GourResource.gsl_b05", "source": {"gour": {"ref": "Thm 11.4 (where it is used; the bridge has no counterpart in the source (foundation))", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.05474v2#nameddest=theorem.11.4", "page": 504}, "hy": [{"ref": "Lemma S2 (for comparison)", "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2408.02722v3#Thmtheorem2a"}]}, "statement": "For a linear isometric isomorphism $U$ between a finite-dimensional space and the standard-model space, for each $n$ there is an isomorphism $U_n$ between the $n$-copy space and the $n$-fold tensor product of the standard model, and the same $U_n$ transports the tensor powers of all states corresponding under $U$.", "book": "Correspondence with finite-dimensional models: isometric transport of tensor powers [foundation; no separate theorem number]", "original": {"gour": "\\begin{myt}{\\color{yellow} The Generalized Quantum Stein's Lemma}\n\\begin{theorem}\\label{gsl}\nLet $\\mf$ be a QRT whose sets of free states satisfy the properties above.\nThen, for all $\\eps\\in(0,1)$ and all $\\rho\\in\\md(A)$\n\\be\\label{1158}\n\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{1}{n}D_{\\min}^{\\eps}\\left(\\rho^{\\otimes n}\\big\\|\\mf\\right)=D^{\\reg}(\\rho\\|\\mf)\\;.\n\\ee\n\\end{theorem}", "hy": "T_{n}\\coloneqq\\qty{ \\rho_n \\geq e^{n (\\underline{R}+\\epsilon_4)} \\sigma_n},\n\\end{align}\nwhich satisfies the condition\n\\begin{align}\n    \\Tr[\\qty(\\mathds{1}-T_{n})\\rho_n] \\leq \\epsilon_3\n\\end{align}\nfor every $n \\ge n_0$.\nSince it holds for all $\\rho_n$ that\n\\begin{align}\n\\Tr[\\qty{ \\rho_n \\geq e^{n (\\underline{R}+\\epsilon_4)} \\sigma_n} \\qty(e^{-n (\\underline{R}+\\epsilon_4)}\\rho_n-\\sigma_{n})]\n\\ge 0,\n\\end{align}\nwe have\n\\begin{align}\n\\beta_{\\epsilon_3} \\left(\\rho_n\\middle\\| \\sigma_{n}\\right)\\leq\\Tr[T_{n}\\sigma_{n} ]\n\\le \\Tr[T_{n} \\qty(e^{-n (\\underline{R}+\\epsilon_4)} \\rho_n) \n]\n\\le e^{-n (\\underline{R}+\\epsilon_4)},\n\\end{align}\nwhich implies\n\\begin{align}\n\\underline{R}+\\epsilon_4\n\\le -\\frac{1}{n} \\log \\beta_{\\epsilon_3} \\left(\\rho_n\\middle\\| \\sigma_{n}\\right) \n\\end{align}\nfor every $n \\ge n_0$.\nThis contradicts~\\eqref{BI3}."}, "signature_sha256": "7b34f6c04dcdc6e0406edda8a0df3db01b533542aeb3201f151c91a5413e292f", "display": {"section": "foundation", "statement": "For a linear isometric isomorphism $U$ between a finite-dimensional space and the standard-model space, for each $n$ there is an isomorphism $U_n$ between the $n$-copy space and the $n$-fold tensor product of the standard model, and the same $U_n$ transports the tensor powers of all states corresponding under $U$."}, "numbered_source": false}
